WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.790
By about the 10th century, four
Sunni schools of law were settled.

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.970
Many later jurists spoke
of a gate that had closed:

3
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:12.490
the gate of ijtihad, fresh
reasoning from the sources.

4
00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.890
But new questions keep arriving.

5
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:15.900
Banking.

6
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.160
IVF.

7
00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.320
Tobacco.

8
00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.570
So was that gate really shut?

9
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.310
And who wants it open?

10
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:25.550
In this mission, you'll compare
Sunni and Shi'a answers,

11
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.090
side by side.

12
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:30.040
Then you'll meet two
reformers: Rashid Rida,

13
00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:34.090
who edited a journal in
Cairo, and Abdullahi An-Na'im,

14
00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:35.730
a professor of law.

15
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.710
Your mission: find out whether
the gate ever really closed,

16
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.090
and who wants it open.
